# Documentation

**Agents:** topic truth lives in glob-scoped `.cursor/rules/<topic>.mdc` — not `docs/`, not duplicated narratives.

**Human (maintainer):** keep **one** living file — [`MAINTAINER.md`](../../MAINTAINER.md). For now its job is an **up-to-date description of the Sveltia effort** (what we’re doing, where we are, what’s next). Update it in the same session when that story changes. Do not grow a second maintainer doc.

## What goes in a topic rule

- **Must preserve** — invariants the code must not break (match `content_lint` / production build where possible).
- **Stable reference** — ids, mappings, field shapes that rarely change (e.g. `republication` nest).
- **Layout / flow** — only while a UI is still settling; remove once obvious from one component.

## What does NOT go in rules

- **Code maps** (file → concern tables) — drift immediately; use search.
- **Pipeline prose** longer than one line — infer from scripts and workflows.
- **A second doc file** for the same topic — guarantees staleness.

## Other locations

| Location | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `MAINTAINER.md` | **You** — current Sveltia effort (only human living doc) |
| `.cursor/rules/` | Agent invariants (incl. never commit) |
| `README.md` | Author content ops (Italian); not CMS-first until a plan says so |
| `.cursor/plans/` | Pending actionable work only |
| `.cursor/ideas/` | Options and explorations — not shipped truth |
| `_plugins/content_lint.rb` | Executable content contracts |
| `_review/` | One-shot handoff briefs (not living topic docs) |

## When you change a domain

Edit **one** `.mdc` rule in the same session. If an invariant moved into lint/tests, delete it from the rule. Refresh `MAINTAINER.md` if the Sveltia story (status / next) changed. Do not add or update `docs/<topic>.md`.
